  "sourceBase": "c83bd7c197b134a594f6bfe33db411970c26cef7",
  "scope": "0.11.0-claudegpt.31: the cutover release. The managed Windows release is the native WPF shell (wpf/Reframe.Shell, packaged by maintenance/package-shell.ps1 from CI's reframe-shell and reframe-host artifacts) with the Rust PTY host (rust/reframe-host); no Electron file ships. Stage 4 parity (S4b session creation and control, S4c startup auto-resume, model suggestions, WSL running-elsewhere check) and S14 (profile/route resolution, --quit, entry points, packaged smoke). PTY host protocol unchanged. Live cutover qualified on a throwaway profile: Electron 0.10.1-claudegpt.30's Node host sessions survived Electron --quit, were attached by the shell without respawn, survived the shell's --quit and were taken back by Electron .30 (same host and session pids). Inputs: shipped sources (src, rust, wpf, maintenance) changed since 0.10.1-claudegpt.30 (ecdf592), the protocol and cutover docs, the version and release notes.",
